  "description": "Third-party maintained .NET 10 WPF runtime replacement with a D3D11 rendering backend for win-x64 and win-arm64. Not an official Microsoft product; not endorsed by Microsoft. Pinned to WPF 10.0.14. Experimental color Emoji is opt-in. wpfgfx FileVersion 10.1.0.4; all other runtime payload bytes preserved from 10.0.14-d3d11.3.",
  "id": "WpfD3D11Runtime",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-24T02:08:42.48Z",
  "licenseFile": "LICENSE.txt",
  "licenseUrl": "https://aka.ms/deprecateLicenseUrl",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "FtyTbHf0OZ3cwpE0EKzmjGF0VNuj/sAis3yNRURBS/FSt78cPPipVQqTCtwa1HqDVjbHq0jaq0/p+Q48WsKKpw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 38634719,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/QuickerOrg/wpf",
  "published": "2026-11-24T02:04:49.24Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.0.14-d3d11.4 adds experimental color Emoji, disabled by default: set QUICKER_WPF_COLOR_GLYPHS=1 before WPF loads. Background prewarming is enabled with color; set QUICKER_WPF_COLOR_GLYPHS_PREWARM=0 to disable it. Optional disk caching requires QUICKER_WPF_COLOR_GLYPHS_DISK_CACHE to name an existing directory; QUICKER_WPF_RT_TIMING_LOG enables diagnostics. Startup work is reduced by physical-device and shader reuse and embedded precompiled shaders; bounded glyph caching, scale-animation reuse, complex-sequence prewarming and a prewarming retry fix are included. Segoe UI Emoji COLRv1 was validated; COLRv0, SVG and bitmap fonts are not covered. Multi-adapter and device-loss behavior is not tested. Qualcomm sampling truncation remains. Only wpfgfx is rebuilt (FileVersion 10.1.0.4); other runtime files retain the signed .3 bytes and versions. Shared-framework servicing does not automatically update bundled runtime files. Source: 5857e5be84e68c813986709db2dbb1e4488183ad.",
